{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q020_syntaxin_fragment_reclassification","answer":"SCOPe 2.08 treats the early structures as incomplete examples of the syntaxin domain, not evidence for a separate spectrin-like evolutionary lineage. Both 1br0 (d1br0a_, SUNID 17772) and 1ez3 (e.g. d1ez3a_, SUNID 17768) retain the annotation “three-helical fragment; similar to one spectrin repeat” and an ms flag for missing secondary structures comprising less than one-third of the common domain. They are classified with 1dn1 chain B (d1dn1b_) in the t-snare proteins family a.47.2.1, superfamily a.47.2, STAT-like fold a.47, and all-alpha class a. The fold description specifies four long helices.

Thus the full-domain structure should supersede an interpretation based only on the fragments’ three-helix resemblance: incomplete coverage can conceal the architecture needed for a correct fold assignment. Family and superfamily placement support evolutionary relationships within the t-snare group; a shared STAT-like fold establishes structural similarity, not by itself common ancestry with STAT proteins or STAT-related function. Likewise, resemblance to a spectrin repeat does not establish spectrin homology or justify transferring spectrin function.

For whole-domain modeling or fold representatives, prefer a complete, appropriately validated structure; use the fragments only for the regions they actually cover. SCOPe records that 1dn1 was superseded by 3c98 and annotates d1dn1b_ as an automated match to d3c98b_, so current template selection should examine that replacement. The reclassification corrects interpretation of incomplete structural evidence; it does not demonstrate a biological fold switch.","evidence_used":["mcp__scope__get_scop_service_info","mcp__scope__search_scop","mcp__scope__get_scop_node","mcp__scope__get_scop_pdb_entry","mcp__scope__get_scop_domains","/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=Syntaxin&mode=auto&limit=30","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/47663/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/47654/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dn1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dn1/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1br0a_","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1br0a_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1ez3a_","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1ez3a_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dn1b_","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dn1b_/annotations"]}]}
